//OUT="01 11 21 |"

// Every other levelled case nests one `for` in another, or uses `while true`.
// This one mixes them, which is where the two lowerings differ: a `for` becomes
// `while has_next() { i = next(); body }`, so its advance sits at the *top* of
// the body. `cnt 2` jumps to the end of that body, which lands before the
// condition is re-tested and therefore before the next `next()` — the outer
// loop advances exactly once, and `x` is never reached.

fn main
    for i 0..3
        k = 0
        while k < 3
            k++
            out "{i}{k} "
            cnt 2
        out "x"
    out "|"
